    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0157" n="87" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg87"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 248.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 9, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 24th of April, No.
                    146, has been received. Your proceeding in asking from the British government
                    the restoration of the prize ship Emily St. Pierre is approved, equally for its
                    promptness <pb facs="0158" n="88" xml:id="pg88"/> and the grounds upon which it
                    was adopted. The President does not allow himself to doubt that the claim will
                    receive early and just consideration.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
